# Control Flow

Control the execution flow using conditionals and loops.

### Conditionals
```c
if (age >= 18) {
    printf("Adult\n");
} else {
    printf("Minor\n");
}
```

### Loops
- **for loop**:
```c
for (int i = 0; i < 5; i++) {
    printf("%d ", i);
}
```
- **while loop**:
```c
while (count > 0) {
    count--;
}
```
- **do-while loop**: Executes at least once.

# Structures

Structures allow you to group variables of different types under a single name.

### Definition
```c
struct Person {
    char name[50];
    int age;
    float height;
};
```

### Usage
```c
struct Person p1 = {"Alice", 30, 5.7};
printf("%s is %d years old", p1.name, p1.age);
```
